    "body": "## Pull request overview\n\nAdds a CI guardrail to ensure the VS Code recommended extensions list stays identical to the devcontainer’s VS Code extensions list, preventing drift between local editor setup and devcontainer setup.\n\n**Changes:**\n- Added a new regress test/job (`regress-vscode-exts`) that compares `.vscode/extensions.json` recommendations against `.devcontainer/devcontainer.json` extensions.\n- Updated `.vscode/extensions.json` recommendations to match the devcontainer extension list (swap out Solargraph for Dev Containers).\n- Regenerated `.github/workflows/regress.yml` to include the new job in CI.\n\n### Reviewed changes\n\nCopilot reviewed 3 out of 3 changed files in this pull request and generated 2 comments.\n\n| File | Description |\n| ---- | ----------- |\n| tools/test/regress-tests.yaml | Adds a new regress test that asserts devcontainer and recommended VS Code extensions match. |\n| .vscode/extensions.json | Updates recommended extensions to align with devcontainer extensions. |\n| .github/workflows/regress.yml | Regenerated CI workflow to run the new extension-sync check. |\n\n\n\n\n\n---\n\n💡 <a href=\"/riscv/riscv-unified-db/new/main?filename=.github/instructions/*.instructions.md\" class=\"Link--inTextBlock\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Add Copilot custom instructions</a> for smarter, more guided reviews. <a href=\"https://docs.github.com/en/copilot/customizing-copilot/adding-repository-custom-instructions-for-github-copilot\" class=\"Link--inTextBlock\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Learn how to get started</a>.",
